                        "form": "yeggs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "90c15e66-1721-356d-b042-85f636bb559b",
                        "entry_id": "be59d347-8b28-3f6a-81cb-a3a123f0e7ef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who breaks open safes; a burglar."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "87d37fa8-6148-4b43-b092-eccdd1c9f22a",
                                "sense_id": "90c15e66-1721-356d-b042-85f636bb559b",
                                "text": "1904, Edwin S. Porter (director), Capture of the ‘Yegg’ Bank Burglars"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ab7e993-0c11-40c9-8d7b-150ae62ea715",
                                "sense_id": "90c15e66-1721-356d-b042-85f636bb559b",
                                "text": "She was frankly disappointed. For some reason she had expected to discover a burglar of one or another accepted type—either a dashing cracksman in full-blown evening dress, lithe, polished, pantherish, or a common yegg, a red-eyed, unshaven, burly brute in the rags and tatters of a tramp."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f80466dd-988f-4439-9928-fc8cae10ca65",
                                "sense_id": "90c15e66-1721-356d-b042-85f636bb559b",
                                "text": "‘These racketeers are a new type. We think about them the way we think about old time yeggs or needled-up punks.’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0cbaff45-69b6-4e88-998b-51c7706060cc",
                        "source_entry_id": "be59d347-8b28-3f6a-81cb-a3a123f0e7ef",
